          "en": "The boat slides out from the steps. “And you?” the boatman asks Dādī. “And you, little one?” he asks the spirit. The spirit cannot answer: no one has ever said “you” to him and meant it. Dādī says it first: a clear, kind word, aimed straight at him.",
